{
  "base": "9bf8bf3e",
  "claims": [
    "GO3-C1/C2: narrow_proposal keeps exactly the admitted and unassessed operations, drops refused-* and dropped-with ones and re-runs GO2's closure over any outcome list; the narrowed proposal previews and applies like any other.",
    "GO3-C3/R0.3: the narrowed proposal has its own proposal_id and narrowed_from; a proposal without narrowed_from keeps its bytes and proposal_sha256 under every schema version; narrowing writes nothing.",
    "GO3 refusals: anything but a proposal and a preview/outcome report, another proposal's outcomes, a preview with no outcomes, a before model that is not expected_model_sha256, or rows that do not cover the operations, each by name in that order.",
    "GO5-C1..C3: the summary's proposed total equals the sum of outcomes when present; added comes from the evolution record only; reused and host drops are the round file's, reported verbatim; every artifact is bound to the one before it.",
    "GO5 round file: the reader refuses an oversize file, NaN, deep nesting, a huge integer, an extra or duplicate key and a duplicate reused row, each as RoundFileError; gnd evolve summary exits 3 on a refusal with nothing on stdout, and 64 on a usage error.",
    "GO2 r2 repairs: _needs reads a reference key only where the ORM meta-schema declares that property (never in a sample row or provenance), depends_on included; a role step by position or name is located; a constraint issue is never pinned on a host-only change; the constraint index is linear.",
    "GO4 r1 repairs: the guard fails when any rule sentence is reversed, deleted or narrowed, or hidden in an HTML comment, and passes on equivalent Markdown (unpadded tables, closed headings, tilde fences, reflowed lines); the page no longer tells a host to write facts against an existing fact type.",
    "Every regular expression, string split, slice and special-case branch this change adds handles the whole class of input it is given, not only the examples in the tests and fixtures, and none reads structured text that a parser or an existing reader in this repository already reads."
  ],
